    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/rivieredu/jobs/5435175/affiliated-faculty-forensic-science": {
      "title": "Affiliated Faculty, Forensic Science",
      "description": "Affiliated Faculty, Forensic Science Location Nashua Job Type Part-Time Job Number 202500231 Division Division of Arts and Sciences Department Biology Opening Date 08/04/2026 Description Benefits Description Affiliated Faculty – Forensic Science Appointment Type: Affiliated Faculty Reports To: Vice President for Academic Affairs Classification: Non-tenure, part-time, paid position, hybrid work location, non-benefits eligible Role Summary Affiliated Faculty in Forensic Science serve as externally engaged academic professionals who contribute to the intellectual vitality, market relevance, and sustainability of University programs. This role is designed for accomplished professionals who maintain active engagement in industry, government, or applied research environments and who leverage those relationships to support high-quality teaching, enrollment growth, and workforce-aligned education. Duties and Responsibilities Primary Responsibilities 1. Instructional Contributions Teach undergraduate courses in forensic science and the sciences integrating industry practices, tools, and ethical considerations. Support applied learning experiences such as internships and capstone projects. Advise and mentor students on career pathways, certifications, professional practice, and ethical leadership in technology. Promote responsible and human-centered approaches to forensic science and the sciences. 2. Program Growth and Enrollment Support Actively support student recruitment and enrollment growth through outreach, referral, and professional visibility. Participate in informational sessions, open houses, webinars, or employer-facing events as requested. Identify prospective students through professional networks and refer qualified candidates to admissions. 3. Serve as a University Ambassador Identify potential leads for adjunct faculty and partnership opportunities. Maintain a commitment to enrollment growth and program sustainability. Engage in are considered core components of the affiliated faculty role. Maintain active professional involvement in relevant industries Strategic Role of Affiliated Faculty The Affiliated Faculty model enables the University to: Engage students Strengthen enrollment pipelines Deepen industry partnerships Maintain curricular relevance in rapidly evolving technical fields Align academic offerings with workforce and societal needs in forensic science and the sciences. Qualifications The successful candidate will have a demonstrated ability to communicate the value of Rivier’s academic programs, teach on-campus courses over the course of an academic year, support students through advising and internships, and participate in several on-campus recruitment and enrollment related events. This affiliated faculty appointment is designed for working professionals with hybrid or flexible work that allow for regular on-campus instruction and student engagement. Successful applicants will have an earned master’s degree with a doctoral degree preferred. Compensation is based on credits taught, student internship supervision, and measurable contributions that enhance program visibility, brand awareness, and growth enrollment. Supplemental Information Applicants should apply online and include a cover letter along with resume/CV at: https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/rivieredu/jobs/5435175/affiliated-faculty-forensic-science All applications and nominations will be considered highly confidential. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Rivier University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, age, veteran or marital status, sex sexual orientation, gender identity, or disability in admission or access to, treatment in, or employment in its programs and activities, and Title IX requires that the University not discriminate on the bases stated above. This position is not eligible for benefits. Employer Rivier University (NH) Address 420 South Main Street Nashua, New Hampshire, 03060 Phone 603-897-8717 603-897-8211 Website https://www.rivier.edu/ Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/rivieredu/jobs/5470569/assistant-director-of-student-accounts": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Student Accounts",
      "description": "Assistant Director of Student Accounts Location Nashua Job Type Full-Time Job Number 202500239 Division Finance and Administration Department Student Accounts Opening Date 09/02/2026 Description Benefits Description Position: Assistant Director of Student Accounts Department: Student Financial Services Department Reports to: Director of Student Accounts Classification: Exempt Position Type and Expected Hours of Work: Full-time, M-F, 8:30 – 5:00, overtime expected during periods of high activity Travel: 2% and sometimes overnight Summary/Objective: Reporting to the Director, the Assistant Director is tasked with reviewing, coordinating, and performing various professional accounting tasks related to tuition and fee assessment, student billing, and collections. This position assists in managing the day-to-day operations of the office, maintaining compliance, and ensuring a high level of customer service to students and parents. The office is reflective of the overall mission of the University. Duties and Responsibilities · Contributes to the overall success of the Student Accounts Office by supporting all aspects of student billing and collections, loans, receivables and cashiering functions and maintaining compliance. · Assists with ensuring all Student Account Office representatives are consistently providing exemplary customer service to internal and external customers such as parents, students, staff and third parties. · Responsible for overseeing the day-to-day operations of the Student Account Office in the absence of the Director of Student Accounts and providing exemplary customer service. · Responsible for cashier functions including the security of funds, proper recording, timely depositing, petty cash, and reconciliation of cash receipts. · Review student accounts for authorization of bookstore advances and resolves complex billing discrepancies. · Assists with the continued training and development of current student account office team members as well as the training and onboarding of new team members. · Responsible for third-party billing, employee tuition waivers, and commuter, faculty, and staff meal plan administration. · Monitors TouchNet payment plans and payments for ACH returns, failed payments, and plan defaults. · Assists with updating tuition and fee tables and posting transactions to the general ledger. · Processes refunds, ensuring compliance with Federal Title IV regulations. · Maintains functional expertise on the Colleague, Atrium, and Insights systems and promotes technology initiatives to support student self-service. · Assists with maintaining documentation of all policies and procedures and the content of the Student Accounts Office website. · Reviews outstanding receivables with the Director and executes methods for resolution of uncollectible accounts. · Produces monthly, quarterly, and yearly reports and analyses. · Demonstrates excellent organizational skills and ability to manage multiple projects in a fast-paced environment. · Assists the Director in maintaining accuracy and compliance with University, federal and state regulations and guidelines including but not limited to FERPA, Title IV and IRS required filings related to 1098T. · Monitors consistent adherence to University internal control policies and updates existing policies and procedures to implement industry standards. · Responsible for the accuracy, security, and integrity of confidential data within the area. · Creates and maintains a secure office environment to protect all information resources. Qualifications Qualifications: · Bachelor of Science Degree in Business Administration or related field is required. · At least 3 years of progressively responsible professional experience in a business office · Experience working in the Student Accounts or Financial Aid office of a higher education institution is preferred with familiarity in Title IV regulations. · Demonstrated knowledge of the principles, policies, procedures and standards in cash management and accounts receivable. · Experience in resolution of complaints and disputes; demonstrated ability to balance adherence to policies with a need to support student success. · Proficiency with Microsoft Office including Word and Excel, higher education ERP with Colleague experience is a plus. · Understands the commitment to the Rivier University mission of Transforming Hearts and Minds to Serve the World. · A commitment to diversity, equity, inclusion and access in staffing, and student recruitment and retention initiatives. Knowledge and Skills: · Self-starter, ability to communicate effectively in written and oral form. · Strong interpersonal skills with ability to advocate for and support the academic, personal, and professional needs of the University. · Ability to collaborate with faculty and staff and maintain collegial relations. · Flexibility and adaptability in an emerging and changing environment. · Ability to maintain confidentiality and manage confidential information. Physical Demands: · The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. · While performing the duties of this job, the employee is regularly required to talk or hear. The employee frequently is required to stand; walk; use hands to finger, handle or feel; and reach with hands and arms. · This position requires the ability to occasionally lift office products and supplies, up to 20 pounds. This is not necessarily an exhaustive list of all responsibilities, duties, skills, efforts, requirements or working conditions associated with this job. While this is intended to be an accurate reflection of the current job, management reserves the right to revise the job or to require that other or different tasks be performed as assigned. Supplemental Information Applicants should apply online and include a cover letter along with resume/CV at: https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/rivieredu/jobs/5470569/assistant-director-of-student-accounts All applications and nominations will be considered highly confidential. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Rivier University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, age, veteran or marital status, sex sexual orientation, gender identity, or disability in admission or access to, treatment in, or employment in its programs and activities, and Title IX requires that the University not discriminate on the bases stated above. In addition to a competitive salary, Rivier University offers full-time employees a comprehensive benefits package which includes medical, dental and vision coverage, employer paid life and disability plans, retirement plan with employer match, Health Reimbursement Arrangement (HRA), Health Savings Account (HSA) with employer contribution, flexible spending accounts, paid time off, holidays, educational assistance benefits, employee assistance program (EAP) and a variety of additional discounts and services. To learn more details, vist our Summary of Benefits . Employer Rivier University (NH) Address 420 South Main Street Nashua, New Hampshire, 03060 Phone 603-897-8717 603-897-8211 Website https://www.rivier.edu/ Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/rivieredu/jobs/5453515/director-of-counseling-services": {
      "title": "Director of Counseling Services",
      "description": "Director of Counseling Services Location Nashua Job Type Full-Time Job Number 202500238 Division Student Experience Department Counseling and Wellness Opening Date 08/19/2026 Description Benefits Description Position Title: Director of Counseling Services Department: Student Experience Reports to: Dean of Students Classification: Exempt Position Type and Expected Hours of Work: Full time, Monday through Friday Travel: None Summary/Objective: The Director provides leadership and oversight of Student Counseling Services and the delivery of comprehensive mental health services for Rivier students. Responsibilities include individual and group counseling, crisis intervention, coordination of care related to acute mental health concerns and hospitalization, and the development and implementation of prevention, education, outreach, and programming initiatives that support student well-being and success. The Director is responsible for the hiring, supervision, and development of clinical staff and collaborates closely with faculty, staff, students, and external partners to promote a healthy and supportive campus environment. The Director also provides direct clinical services as capacity allows and serves as the University's leading mental health professional, offering advocacy, consultation, vision, and strategic leadership for student mental health at Rivier University. This is a 40-week position, spanning from the second week of August through the third week of May. Counseling services are typically provided only when the University is in session and are not generally scheduled during periods when classes are not in session, such as academic breaks, holiday periods, recesses, and other scheduled closures. Participation in select University events occurring outside of the 40-week schedule, such as New Student Orientation, Accepted Students Days, Open Houses, trainings, and other assigned duties, may be required. Time worked beyond the 40-week appointment will be compensated through a mutually agreed-upon time exchange arrangement. Exact dates and expectations are subject to change based on institutional needs and will be communicated in advance whenever possible. Duties and Responsibilities Consistent with the Principles of Good Practice for Student Affairs at Catholic Colleges and Universities (ACCU), provide vision, strategic planning, and assessment for Student Counseling Services to advance departmental, divisional, and University mission and goals. Direct and oversee the overall operations of Student Counseling Services, including supervision of staff, budget management, and administrative functions; develop and modify programs, services, and delivery methods in accordance with student needs, institutional objectives, and available resources. Provide a full range of short-term personal, emotional, and social counseling services for students, including emergency and crisis intervention services; make referrals to university and community resources as appropriate and maintain all related clinical records. Exercise full supervisory authority and provide clinical supervision for professional staff counselors and graduate interns; conduct performance evaluations and support professional development. Provide referral and crisis intervention services to students as needed, coordinate and support suicide prevention and intervention efforts across the campus community. Provide consultation on campus and within the community regarding student mental health concerns; provide leadership and vision for Rivier in addressing emerging national and campus trends through prevention, education, outreach, and harm-reduction initiatives that support student development and well-being. Develop, implement, and administer center policies, protocols, and procedures in accordance with current national and regional best practices for college counseling centers. Coordinate Student Counseling Services' emergency and crisis response procedures and participate in university behavioral intervention, bias intervention, CARES, and threat assessment activities. Provide training each semester for students, faculty, and staff on pertinent counseling and mental health topics, such as bystander intervention, suicide awareness, stress management, and other student well-being initiatives. Collaborate with colleagues across the University to develop strategies that optimize student strengths, promote healthy development, and support prevention and intervention efforts related to psychological and behavioral concerns. Maintain relationships with off-campus mental health providers, hospitals, and community organizations; develop and implement procedures that ensure continuity of care following psychiatric hospitalization or other higher levels of care. Co-Chair the Alcohol, Tobacco, and Other Drugs (ATOD) Task Force, ensuring compliance with the Drug-Free Schools and Communities Act (DFSCA), including completion of the biennial review and all related regulatory requirements. Maintain and regularly update Student Counseling Services' website and social media platforms. Confer regularly with the Dean of Students, University administrators, faculty, staff, parents, community healthcare providers, and other stakeholders to plan, coordinate, evaluate, and improve services and programs. Maintain a close working relationship with Student Health Services; consult on cases, make referrals as appropriate, and ensure information sharing is conducted in accordance with professional standards and confidentiality requirements. Provide and/or coordinate on-call and after-hours services and crisis interventions as required. Ensure compliance with applicable federal and state laws, professional ethical standards, licensure requirements, and University policies governing counseling services and student records. Represent the University through participation in professional organizations, community partnerships, and national associations. Participate in student recruitment, admissions, accepted student, orientation, and family engagement programs, as requested. Serve on University committees and task forces assigned. Perform other administrative, clinical, and related duties as assigned. Qualifications Qualifications Master’s Level clinician (LICSW, LCMHC) and a minimum of five years of post-licensure clinical and supervisory experience is required. Preference given to candidates with experience in a higher education setting. Valid clinical licensure in current state, with the ability to obtain licensure in New Hampshire. Experience in current college mental health issues including familiarity with the diversity treatment modalities commonly used with this population. Experience supervising and evaluating clinical staff. Demonstrated commitment to inclusive excellence, with the ability to build meaningful relationships and work effectively with students, faculty, staff, and external partners from diverse backgrounds, cultures, and identities. Experience with administrative duties and functions such as strategic planning, developing, and implementing policies and procedures, budget planning and managing resources, and report writing. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Demonstrated ability to respond effectively and compassionately in crisis situations, exercising sound clinical judgment, professionalism, and sensitivity. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to gather, interpret, and evaluate data and information from a variety of sources to inform decision-making, planning, and recommendations. Excellent interpersonal, written, oral, presentation, and public speaking skills, with the ability to communicate effectively with students, faculty, staff, families, and community partners. Ability to establish priorities, manage multiple responsibilities and competing demands, and successfully oversee a complex and dynamic counseling operation. Demonstrated supervisory and leadership experience, including the ability to recruit, develop, mentor, and evaluate staff while fostering a collaborative, inclusive, and high-performing team environment. Ability to build relationships, develop partnerships, and work collaboratively across departments and with external stakeholders to advance student well-being and institutional goals. Strong understanding of the developmental, emotional, and mental health needs of college students and the application of evidence-based prevention, intervention, and support strategies. Knowledge of current best practices, ethical standards, legal requirements, and emerging trends in higher education mental health and college counseling. Demonstrated commitment to maintaining the highest standards of personal and professional integrity, ethical practice, and respect for privacy and confidentiality. Supplemental Information Applicants should apply online and include a cover letter along with resume/CV at: https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/rivieredu/jobs/5453515/director-of-counseling-services All applications and nominations will be considered highly confidential. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Rivier University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, age, veteran or marital status, sex sexual orientation, gender identity, or disability in admission or access to, treatment in, or employment in its programs and activities, and Title IX requires that the University not discriminate on the bases stated above. In addition to a competitive salary, Rivier University offers full-time employees a comprehensive benefits package which includes medical, dental and vision coverage, employer paid life and disability plans, retirement plan with employer match, Health Reimbursement Arrangement (HRA), Health Savings Account (HSA) with employer contribution, flexible spending accounts, paid time off, holidays, educational assistance benefits, employee assistance program (EAP) and a variety of additional discounts and services. To learn more details, vist our Summary of Benefits . Employer Rivier University (NH) Address 420 South Main Street Nashua, New Hampshire, 03060 Phone 603-897-8717 603-897-8211 Website https://www.rivier.edu/ Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/rivieredu/jobs/5220625/faculty-computer-science-ai-program-coordinator": {
      "title": "Faculty, Computer Science & AI - Program Coordinator",
      "description": "Faculty, Computer Science & AI - Program Coordinator Location Nashua Job Type Full-Time Job Number 202500183 Division Division of Arts and Sciences Department Computer Science Opening Date 02/01/2026 Description Benefits Description Coordinator, Computer Science and Artificial Intelligence Program Rivier University invites applications for the position of Coordinator of the Computer Science and Artificial Intelligence (CS/AI) Program . The Coordinator will provide academic leadership, program oversight, and industry-informed guidance for Rivier’s undergraduate and graduate programs in Computer Science and Artificial Intelligence. This role blends teaching, curriculum development, student mentoring, and the creation of substantial external partnership building to ensure that Rivier’s CS/AI programs remain innovative and aligned with evolving industry needs. The ideal candidate brings broad industry experience, a strong professional network, and a demonstrated commitment to excellence in technology education. Duties and Responsibilities Program Leadership and Coordination · Oversee the planning, development, delivery, and continuous improvement of Computer Science and AI programs. · Lead curriculum review and advancement to ensure academic quality and industry alignment. · Coordinate course scheduling, adjunct faculty assignments, and program assessment activities. · Maintain compliance with institutional policies and accreditation standards. Teaching and Student Engagement · Teach courses in Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence, Data Science, or related fields at the undergraduate and/or graduate level. · Advise and mentor students academically and professionally. · Support recruitment, retention, and student success initiatives. Industry and Community Partnerships · Cultivate and sustain relationships with employers, research partners, and industry leaders. · Facilitate internship pathways, experiential learning, and applied project opportunities. · Bring real-world insights and industry trends into program design and classroom instruction. Strategic Advancement · Collaborate with faculty and university leadership to expand the visibility and impact of CS/AI programs. · Support initiatives related to grants, innovation labs, workforce development, or emerging technologies. · Represent Rivier University at professional conferences, events, and regional partnerships. Qualifications · Doctorate degree in a relevant field, or a master’s degree in a relevant field with commensurate industry experience reflecting advanced expertise. · A robust professional network in technology, AI, or related domains. · Experience with curriculum development and program coordination. · Background in applied AI, machine learning, cloud computing, cybersecurity, or software architecture. · Evidence of effective teaching · Strong communication and collaboration skills. Supplemental Information Applicants should apply online and include a cover letter along with resume/CV at: https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/rivieredu/jobs/5220625/faculty-computer-science-ai-program-coordinator All applications and nominations will be considered highly confidential. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Rivier University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, age, veteran or marital status, sex sexual orientation, gender identity, or disability in admission or access to, treatment in, or employment in its programs and activities, and Title IX requires that the University not discriminate on the bases stated above. In addition to a competitive salary, Rivier University offers full-time employees a comprehensive benefits package which includes medical, dental and vision coverage, employer paid life and disability plans, retirement plan with employer match, Health Reimbursement Arrangement (HRA), Health Savings Account (HSA) with employer contribution, flexible spending accounts, paid time off, holidays, educational assistance benefits, employee assistance program (EAP) and a variety of additional discounts and services. To learn more details, vist our Summary of Benefits . Employer Rivier University (NH) Address 420 South Main Street Nashua, New Hampshire, 03060 Phone 603-897-8717 603-897-8211 Website https://www.rivier.edu/ Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/rivieredu/jobs/5301137/graduate-assistant-office-of-admissions": {
      "title": "Graduate Assistant - Office of Admissions",
      "description": "Graduate Assistant - Office of Admissions Salary $12.00 Hourly Location Nashua Job Type Part-Time Job Number 202500196 Division Enrollment Management Department Undergraduate Admissions Opening Date 04/08/2026 Description Benefits Description The Graduate Assistant in the Office of Undergraduate Admissions is tasked with supporting the undergraduate admissions team in recruiting and evaluating applicants. We seek an individual who will bring enthusiasm and initiative to a hardworking, collaborative team. Duties and Responsibilities · Work with the Admissions team to manage the application and enrollment process · Communicate with prospective and admitted candidates via telephone, email and text · Meet face-to-face with candidates and conduct informational sessions and campus tours · Assist with communications and marketing to prospective and admitted candidates · Assist with the planning and execution of recruitment and field events · Manage specific projects related to recruitment and enrollment cycles as needed · Assist with other activities as needed · Assist and manage travel events throughout New England Qualifications · Bachelor's degree · Graduate Assistant must be admitted or enrolled in from a Rivier University graduate degree program · Ability to work a flexible schedule that includes some evenings and weekends · Strong interpersonal and writing skills are necessary, including public speaking skills and the ability to represent the University in a positive way to diverse populations. · The ability and willingness to support the mission of the University in all daily activities with a student-centered focus. · Strong skills in computers and technology. Proficient with Microsoft Office applications, particularly Excel and Word. · Basic familiarity with social media applications a plus. · Ability to collaborate as part of a team, but work independently when needed · High attention to detail · Ability to represent the University in a professional manner Supplemental Information Applicants should apply online with resume and cover letter at: https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/rivieredu/jobs/5301137/graduate-assistant-office-of-admissions Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Rivier University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, age, veteran or marital status, sex sexual orientation, gender identity, or disability in admission or access to, treatment in, or employment in its programs and activities, and Title IX requires that the University not discriminate on the bases stated above. Graduate Assistants are eligible for tuition reimbursement of two (2) courses per semester. Employer Rivier University (NH) Address 420 South Main Street Nashua, New Hampshire, 03060 Phone 603-897-8717 603-897-8211 Website https://www.rivier.edu/ Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/rivieredu/jobs/5525011/director-of-undergraduate-nursing-education": {
      "title": "Director of Undergraduate Nursing Education",
      "description": "Director of Undergraduate Nursing Education Location Nashua Job Type Full-Time Job Number 202500243 Division Div of Nursing & Health Professions Department Nursing and Health Professions Opening Date 10/21/2026 Description Benefits Description DIRECTOR OF UNDERGRADUATE NURSING EDUCATION Pre-licensure and Post-Licensure (RN-BS) Programs The Director of Undergraduate Nursing Education, Pre-licensure, and Post-Licensure (RN-BS) Programs is a full-time member of the faculty of the Division of Nursing and Health Professions is responsible for the administration and leadership of these nursing programs. The Director is accountable to the Dean of the Division of Nursing and Health Professions and to the Vice President for Academic Affairs as regards to the Nursing Programs and courses Duties and Responsibilities Overall responsibility - Ensure quality in person and online education as evidenced by continuing accreditation by professional accrediting body, Accreditation Commission for Education in Nursing (ACEN) and State of New Hampshire Board of Nursing approval for prelicensure programs. The areas of responsibilities include curriculum, faculty, students, and ongoing systematic evaluation in undergraduate nursing. Administrative Responsibilities: Provide strategic leadership to the Undergraduate nursing programs (ASN, LPN-ASN, BSN, ABSN, RN-BSN). Support the mission and goals of the University and the Division in articulating these goals and objectives with Divisional colleagues. Plan and conduct regularly scheduled Pre-licensure and as needed, Post-licensure (RNBS) program meetings. Advise the Dean relative to the program status, future directions, and projected needs and resources, including budget. Provide input to the Dean relative to anticipated needs for new faculty and adjuncts Interview and recommend new candidates for faculty positions for undergraduate programs. Monitor Undergraduate Nursing Program quality and implementation. Provide input to the Dean regarding proposed faculty teaching assignments, course offerings, and schedules. Evaluate all full-time faculty who teach in the ASN and BSN nursing programs. Work closely with the Clinical Faculty and Partnership Coordinator to anticipate staffing needs and support the recruitment, selection, and securement of qualified clinical adjunct faculty. Work closely with the Clinical Faculty and Partnership Coordinator to retain and expand clinical agencies. Follow up with Clinical Compliance Administrators in planning clinical assignments and selecting clinical placements for pre-licensure students. Monitor the academic progress of undergraduate nursing students. Provide support and academic advising to undergraduate nursing students. Assist with marketing and recruitment activities pertaining to undergraduate programs in collaboration with the Office of Admissions and nursing faculty and staff. Network with health care organizations and educational institutions and assist in the development of articulation agreements and strategic partnerships. Assist Dean in preparing the Divisional Annual Report. Participate in discussions regarding budget, disciplinary actions, grievance, and evaluation. Serve on Assessment and Evaluation Committee and Admissions Committee. Final considerations of budget, hiring and rehiring of faculty and staff, discipline, grievance, and Divisional faculty evaluation, together with recommendations for promotion and tenure, are the responsibility of the Dean, who is accountable to the Vice President for Academic Affairs for the overall conduct and administration of the Division of Nursing. Curricular Responsibilities: Coordinate the revision of curriculum to meet state (NH), ACEN accreditation and professional nursing standards. Coordinate activities of Divisional committees in monitoring program quality and preparing reports for various accrediting agencies, i.e., University Program Reviews, ACEN, NHBON. Weekend and/or evening appearance at scheduled Admissions events (Accepted Students Day, ASN, BSN and RN-BSN information sessions, Open House). Other duties as required to support the Mission of Rivier University and the Philosophy of the Division of Nursing and Health Professions. Qualifications The Director of Undergraduate Nursing Education will be a full-time administrative position with possible grant responsibilities, holding the academic rank of Assistant Professor or higher. Baccalaureate, master’s degree in nursing, doctoral degree preferred or actively pursuing doctoral study. Strong leadership skills. Supplemental Information Applicants should apply online and include a cover letter along with resume/CV at: https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/rivieredu/jobs/5525011/director-of-undergraduate-nursing-education All applications and nominations will be considered highly confidential. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Rivier University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, age, veteran or marital status, sex sexual orientation, gender identity, or disability in admission or access to, treatment in, or employment in its programs and activities, and Title IX requires that the University not discriminate on the bases stated above. In addition to a competitive salary, Rivier University offers full-time employees a comprehensive benefits package which includes medical, dental and vision coverage, employer paid life and disability plans, retirement plan with employer match, Health Reimbursement Arrangement (HRA), Health Savings Account (HSA) with employer contribution, flexible spending accounts, paid time off, holidays, educational assistance benefits, employee assistance program (EAP) and a variety of additional discounts and services. To learn more details, vist our Summary of Benefits . Employer Rivier University (NH) Address 420 South Main Street Nashua, New Hampshire, 03060 Phone 603-897-8717 603-897-8211 Website https://www.rivier.edu/ Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/rivieredu/jobs/5524665/administrative-assistant-enrollment-management": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant, Enrollment Management",
      "description": "Administrative Assistant, Enrollment Management Location Nashua Job Type Full-Time Job Number 202500242 Division Enrollment Management Department Office of Enrollment Mgmt Opening Date 10/21/2026 Description Benefits Description Provides administrative, operational, data, and event support to the Vice President for Enrollment Management and the Office of Admission. This position is the first point of contact and plays a key role in the recruitment of new students. Duties and Responsibilities Greet and engage with prospective students and their guests providing a welcoming environment. Answer and direct incoming calls to the appropriate person. Demonstrate a high level of customer service and professionalism. Schedule meetings, appointments, and maintain department and Vice President calendars. Maintain and reorder inventory of recruitment materials and office supplies. Responsible for processing invoices for departmental expenditures. Assist with planning and executing events, meetings, and special projects. Perform data entry into Customer Relationship Management (CRM) system. Qualifications Proficient in Microsoft Office (Word, Excel, PowerPoint) and strong data entry skills Experience in managing high-volume work in a fast-paced, deadline-driven environment. Ability to balance multiple short- and long-term tasks effectively Demonstrated integrity, attention to detail, and strong organizational skills Ability to work both independently and collaboratively Bachelor’s Degree preferred Excellent customer service skills Strong writing and communication skills Dynamic analytical and critical thinking skills Detail oriented Ability to Prioritize Supplemental Information Applicants should apply online and include a cover letter along with resume/CV at: https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/rivieredu/jobs/5524665/administrative-assistant-enrollment-management All applications and nominations will be considered highly confidential. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Rivier University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, age, veteran or marital status, sex sexual orientation, gender identity, or disability in admission or access to, treatment in, or employment in its programs and activities, and Title IX requires that the University not discriminate on the bases stated above. In addition to a competitive salary, Rivier University offers full-time employees a comprehensive benefits package which includes medical, dental and vision coverage, employer paid life and disability plans, retirement plan with employer match, Health Reimbursement Arrangement (HRA), Health Savings Account (HSA) with employer contribution, flexible spending accounts, paid time off, holidays, educational assistance benefits, employee assistance program (EAP) and a variety of additional discounts and services. To learn more details, vist our Summary of Benefits . Employer Rivier University (NH) Address 420 South Main Street Nashua, New Hampshire, 03060 Phone 603-897-8717 603-897-8211 Website https://www.rivier.edu/ Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/rivieredu/jobs/5534327/nursing-sim-lab-per-diem-support": {
      "title": "Nursing SIM lab - per diem support",
      "description": "Nursing SIM lab - per diem support Location Nashua Job Type Part-Time Job Number 202500244 Division Div of Nursing & Health Professions Department Nursing and Health Professions Opening Date 10/29/2026 Description Benefits Description Position : Nursing Simulation Specialist Department: Division of Nursing & Health Professions Reports to: Director, Health Professions Resource Center Classification: Non Exempt (Hourly), Per Diem, Temportary- scheduled as needed. Hours are variable and may include evenings and/or weekends. Summary/Objective: Reporting to the DNHP Nursing Simulation Center Director, the Assistant will assist with the management and the day to day coordination of lab activities. Duties and Responsibilities Duties and Responsibilities: Assist with inventory and management of lab supplies. Set up Simulation Labs and skills labs. Monitor Open Labs when work study students are not available. Assist faculty in the Simulation Lab according to the prepared script. Trouble shoot problems with EKG machines, student iPads, computers, equipment and mannequins in the lab and report malfunctions to the Nursing Simulation and Clinical Education Center Director. Assist the Simulation Center Director with any other duties that become necessary. Qualifications LPN, LNA, CNA, MA or a registered nurse preferred. Supplemental Information Applicants should apply online and include a cover letter along with resume/CV at: https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/rivieredu/jobs/5534327/nursing-sim-lab-per-diem-support All applications and nominations will be considered highly confidential. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Rivier University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, age, veteran or marital status, sex sexual orientation, gender identity, or disability in admission or access to, treatment in, or employment in its programs and activities, and Title IX requires that the University not discriminate on the bases stated above. In addition to a competitive salary, Rivier University offers full-time employees a comprehensive benefits package which includes medical, dental and vision coverage, employer paid life and disability plans, retirement plan with employer match, Health Reimbursement Arrangement (HRA), Health Savings Account (HSA) with employer contribution, flexible spending accounts, paid time off, holidays, educational assistance benefits, employee assistance program (EAP) and a variety of additional discounts and services. To learn more details, vist our Summary of Benefits . Employer Rivier University (NH) Address 420 South Main Street Nashua, New Hampshire, 03060 Phone 603-897-8717 603-897-8211 Website https://www.rivier.edu/"
